                <pb facs="0526" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg478"/>

                <head>No. 278.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Shishkin to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Russia</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 26, 1877</date>.
                        (Received June 26.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: His Majesty the Emperor, my august
                    sovereign, deigned to order on the 29th april,/11th May, last, that any vessel
                    sailing under a neutral flag should have the right, during the entire duration
                    of the present war with Turkey, to engage in the coasting trade between the
                    Russian ports of the Black Sea and the Sea of Azov.</p>
                <p>In bringing this decision to the knowledge of the Federal Government, I avail
                    myself of this occasion to beg you, Mr. Secretary of State, to accept the
                    assurance of my very high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>N. SHISHKIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
